"@next/next/no-img-element","Using `<img>` could result in slower LCP and higher bandwidth. Consider using `<Image />` from `next/image` or a custom image loader to automatically optimize images. This may incur additional usage or cost from your provider. See: https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/no-img-element","JSXOpeningElement",["2270"],["2271"],"react-hooks/purity","Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Date.now` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\n/home/gabriel/Documentos/EnergyOS/src/app/liga/page.tsx:54:58\n  52 | function useCountdown(weekEnd: string) {\n  53 |   const calc = (end: string) => {\n> 54 |     const diff = new Date(end + \"T23:59:59\").getTime() - Date.now();\n     |                                                          ^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  55 |     if (diff <= 0) return { days: 0, hours: 0, minutes: 0, seconds: 0 };\n  56 |     return {\n  57 |       days: Math.floor(diff / 86400000),","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\n/home/gabriel/Documentos/EnergyOS/src/app/liga/page.tsx:115:32\n  113 |\n  114 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 115 |     if (!loading && user) void fetchData();\n      |                                ^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  116 |   }, [loading, user, fetchData]);\n  117 |\n  118 |   if (loading || !user) {","'AnimatePresence' is defined but never used.",["2272"],"Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\n/home/gabriel/Documentos/EnergyOS/src/app/loja/page.tsx:136:5\n  134 |\n  135 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 136 |     setHoverCapable(\n      |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  137 |       typeof window !== \"undefined\" && window.matchMedia(\"(hover: hover)\").matches,\n  138 |     );\n  139 |   }, []);","Error: Calling setState synchronously within an effect can trigger cascading renders\n\nEffects are intended to synchronize state between React and external systems such as manually updating the DOM, state management libraries, or other platform APIs. In general, the body of an effect should do one or both of the following:\n* Update external systems with the latest state from React.\n* Subscribe for updates from some external system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\n/home/gabriel/Documentos/EnergyOS/src/app/loja/page.tsx:719:5\n  717 |   useEffect(() => {\n  718 |     if (!user) return;\n> 719 |     fetchStore();\n      |     ^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  720 |     // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps\n  721 |   }, [user?.uid]);\n  722 |","Error: Cannot call impure function during render\n\n`Date.now` is an impure function. Calling an impure function can produce unstable results that update unpredictably when the component happens to re-render. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#components-and-hooks-must-be-idempotent).\n\n/home/gabriel/Documentos/EnergyOS/src/app/loja/page.tsx:746:82\n  744 |   const boostRemaining = useMemo(() => {\n  745 |     if (!store?.xpBoost?.expiresAt) return 0;\n> 746 |     return Math.max(0, Math.floor((new Date(store.xpBoost.expiresAt).getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000));\n      |                                                                                  ^^^^^^^^^^ Cannot call impure function\n  747 |   }, [store?.xpBoost?.expiresAt, boostTick]);\n  748 |\n  749 |   // Deep-link para uma seção (ex.: \"?section=auras\" ao tocar numa aura","React Hook useMemo has an unnecessary dependency: 'boostTick'. Either exclude it or remove the dependency array.",["2273"],"'equippedItem' is assigned a value but never used.","'rc' is assigned a value but never used.",["2274"],["2275"],["2276"],["2277"],["2278"],["2279"],"'MonthlyRecap' is defined but never used.",["2280"],["2281"],"'_amount' is defined but never used.","'_newBalance' is defined but never used.",["2282"],"'scheduleReminder' is defined but never used.",["2283"],"'PERMISSION_KEY' is assigned a value but never used.","'DENIED_KEY' is assigned a value but never used.","'ArrowUpRight' is defined but never used.",["2284"],"'api' is defined but never used.",["2285"],"'PieChart' is defined but never used.",["2286"],"'Pie' is defined but never 